    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `riskFlag` response field on owners: **true when any of** the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity \u2014 otherwise false.\n\nSince these three signals were already computed elsewhere in the pipeline, `riskFlag` is a purely derived response field (like `ownerSegment`, `membershipPoints`, etc.), computed at mapping time so it works for both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `OwnerDto` schema (so the generated DTO carries it).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", expression = RiskFlag.of(owner))`.\n- **`util/RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 OR of the three signals:\n  - possible duplicate \u2192 the entity's existing `possibleDuplicate` flag,\n  - disposable-adjacent email \u2192 `DisposableDomains.isAdjacent(email)`,\n  - over soft capacity \u2192 the entity's existing `capacityWarning` transient (city already holds \u2265 40 owners, the soft threshold below the hard cap of 50).\n- **`util/DisposableDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for the disposable blocklist plus the *adjacency* rule: a domain not itself blocked but sharing its second-level label with a blocked domain (different TLD like `mailinator.net`, or a subdomain like `smtp.mailinator.com`).\n- **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `DisposableDomains` for its exact-match 400 check, so the blocklist isn't duplicated.\n\nInterpretation notes (the spec left two terms open, and only the false case is tested): I read \"disposable-adjacent\" as *near a known disposable domain but not exactly one* (exact matches are already rejected at registration, so a stored owner never has one), and \"over its soft capacity\" as the existing capacity-warning band (\u2265 40, below the hard 50). Both are documented in the new schema field and the util Javadoc.",
